.nh
.TH "PB-RECIPE-REVOKE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recipe-revoke - Revoke a recipe and remove its machines


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recipe revoke <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke a recipe: its token stops working and every machine paired from it is
removed. Without --confirm, print what changes and the confirmation code; run it
again with --confirm <code>\&. Use pb recipe rotate instead to replace a leaked token
and keep the machines.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	the confirmation code printed without --confirm

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recipe revoke ci
  pb recipe revoke ci --confirm 7RT2WD
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recipe(1)\fP
